cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  BSARD RAG Thesis: Corpus Construction and Retrieval-Augmented
  Generation over Belgian Statutory Law
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these
  metadata. Please also cite the underlying BSARD dataset
  (see DATA_LICENSE.md).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Marios
    family-names: Paschalidis
    email: paschalidismarios@gmail.com
    affiliation: KU Leuven
repository-code: "https://github.com/MariusPasch/bsard-rag-thesis"
abstract: >-
  A mono-repo for a master's thesis at KU Leuven on
  retrieval-augmented generation over Belgian statutory law.
  It builds a SQLite corpus database linking 49 Justel
  consolidated Belgian law PDFs to the Belgian Statutory
  Article Retrieval Dataset (BSARD), then evaluates retrieval
  and RAG methods across three research questions: sparse,
  dense, hybrid and agentic retrieval (RQ1); naive,
  metadata-aware and PageIndex retrieval arms (RQ2); and a
  reusable multi-tier retrieval and autonomous evaluation
  harness (RQ3).
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - legal NLP
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - BSARD
  - dense retrieval
  - corpus construction
  - Belgian law
